schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: Seed / Sapling / Canopy local-node maturity model
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    A three-stage growth model for local (place-based) regenerative-finance
    nodes: a Seed node is still building its core team; a Sapling has active
    engagement and real projects; a Canopy node is mature enough to "provide
    shelter and support" to other nodes. New members are framed as
    "seedlings" that the onboarding system helps grow.
  source_traditions:
    - ReFi DAO Local Node Incubator, Beta Cohort Retrospective
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Used in the article both as a description of node-level maturity and as a
    template readers are told to "map your node against" in the closing
    exercise.
  adjacent_meanings:
    - Deployment-readiness ladders (L0 idea → L6 field-informed pattern) used elsewhere in the toolkit's own K1 state model
  important_distinctions:
    - >-
      This is a node-level maturity model (about the whole local chapter),
      distinct from individual member-onboarding stages (observe → first
      contribution → real role) described in the same article.
  tensions: []
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    None flagged — sourced to a named program retrospective, not attributed to
    an unnamed community or tradition.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/onboarding-members.md
    surfaced_by: ReFi DAO Local Node Incubator, Beta Cohort Retrospective
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
